# cp.async with a register src-size, 16 on lanes 0..15 and 0 on the
# others: ptxas writes LDGSTS with an ignore-src predicate. The report
# counts cp-size on every lane, 16–17 sectors per warp and 1024 B per
# CTA, where Nsight Compute measures 8 sectors over the launch.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/cp_async_src_size.ptx --ncu %fixtures/micro/cp_async_src_size.ncu.json | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: global load 16 B   warp: 16–17 sectors (ideal 16)
CHECK: global bytes: load 1024 B, store 0 B
CHECK: measured L2 sectors of global accesses: 0 lines agree (0 exact, 0 within a range, 0 within a bound), 1 differ
CHECK-NEXT: line 30: predicted 32–34 (ideal 32), measured 8 (ideal 8)
